# Mosquitto credentials for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY.
#
# Every password here is `safelock_dev_only`, hashed by `mosquitto_passwd`. It
# is committed on purpose and is safe to commit for exactly the reason the
# Postgres password in docker-compose.yml is: it authenticates a container
# listening on localhost with nothing of value behind it.
#
# **No credential in this file may ever exist in production.** Production
# devices get a per-device credential minted by
# `POST /admin/devices/:id/credential`, shown once, stored only as a `sha256` —
# and the API gets its own privileged credential from the environment. There is
# no fleet password anywhere in the real design, which is why this file lists
# each device separately rather than sharing one.
#
# To add a device to the local fleet:
#   docker compose exec mosquitto mosquitto_passwd -b \
#     /mosquitto/config/passwordfile SAFE-0004 safelock_dev_only
# (then commit the file, since it is mounted read-only)
#
# The ACL in `aclfile` is what makes these identities mean something: a device
# can reach only its own topics, keyed on the username being its serial number.

